---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import CopyCommand from '../components/CopyCommand.astro';
---

<Base
  title="AgentGuard documentation — honest agent security checks"
  description="Install AgentGuard, run an offline static check, and add live behavioural simulation when you need a signed deployment verdict."
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" class="docs">
    <div class="container docs-shell">
      <header class="docs-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
        <h1>From install to an honest gate.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          AgentGuard has two distinct modes. Offline static checks need no account or API key.
          Behavioural simulation runs through a control plane. The output always says which mode
          ran and which coverage is still missing.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="quickstart">
        <div>
          <p class="step">01 · offline quickstart</p>
          <h2 id="quickstart">Run the first check locally</h2>
          <p>
            This validates structure, declared policies, and accidental credentials. It never
            executes a model or tool and never reads your environment variables.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="command-stack">
          <CopyCommand command="pip install agentguard-dev" prompt="$" />
          <CopyCommand command="agentguard init" prompt="$" />
          <CopyCommand command="agentguard scan --local" prompt="$" />
        </div>
        <aside class="boundary">
          <strong>Expected exit: 40 · INCOMPLETE</strong>
          <span>
            Static checks ran, but behavioural scenarios require a live model and are marked
            skipped—not passed. This is a safety property, not an installation failure.
          </span>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="ci">
        <div>
          <p class="step">02 · CI</p>
          <h2 id="ci">Choose the gate you mean</h2>
          <p>
            `agentguard init` writes a GitHub Actions workflow. A team may explicitly accept an
            offline partial gate while it prepares live behavioural simulation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="command-stack">
          <CopyCommand
            command="agentguard scan --local --allow-incomplete-static --sarif findings.sarif"
            prompt="$"
          />
        </div>
        <aside class="boundary warn">
          <strong>`--allow-incomplete-static` means partial coverage</strong>
          <span>It does not turn skipped behavioural scenarios into passes.</span>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="live">
        <div>
          <p class="step">03 · behavioural simulation</p>
          <h2 id="live">Gate a real agent decision</h2>
          <p>
            Run or connect an AgentGuard control plane, then provide its URL, an API key, and the
            registered agent identifier. The model can be challenged while its real tools remain
            intercepted and unexecuted.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>export AGENTGUARD_API_KEY=ag_your_key_here
agentguard scan \
  --api-url https://your-agentguard-host \
  --agent my-support-bot \
  --manifest manifest.json \
  --environment prod \
  --html report.html \
  --sarif findings.sarif</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="codes">
        <div>
          <p class="step">Reference</p>
          <h2 id="codes">Exit-code contract</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="code-grid" role="list">
          <div role="listitem"><code>0</code><span>allowed</span></div>
          <div role="listitem"><code>10</code><span>error</span></div>
          <div role="listitem"><code>20</code><span>blocked</span></div>
          <div role="listitem"><code>30</code><span>unknown</span></div>
          <div role="listitem"><code>40</code><span>incomplete</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="fineprint">
          Fail closed by default: error, blocked, unknown, and incomplete all return non-zero.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .docs-shell { max-width: 900px; padding-block: clamp(56px, 9vw, 112px); }
  .docs-hero { padding-bottom: var(--sp-16); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  h1 { max-width: 13ch; margin-top: var(--sp-4); font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem); line-height: var(--lh-tight); }
  .lede { max-width: 66ch; margin-top: var(--sp-6); color: var(--text); font-size: var(--fs-md); }
  .doc-section { display: grid; min-width: 0; gap: var(--sp-6); padding-block: var(--sp-16); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .doc-section > * { min-width: 0; max-width: 100%; }
  .step { color: var(--brand); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-xs); letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h2 { margin-top: var(--sp-2); font-size: clamp(var(--fs-xl), 4vw, var(--fs-3xl)); }
  h2 + p { max-width: 68ch; margin-top: var(--sp-4); color: var(--text-mut); }
  .command-stack { display: grid; min-width: 0; gap: var(--sp-3); width: 100%; max-width: 680px; }
  .boundary { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-2); padding: var(--sp-5, 20px); color: var(--text); background: var(--info-dim); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--info) 40%, var(--border)); border-radius: var(--r-md); }
  .boundary strong { color: var(--text-hi); }
  .boundary span { color: var(--text-mut); }
  .boundary.warn { background: var(--warn-dim); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 40%, var(--border)); }
  .code-block { overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; padding: var(--sp-6); color: var(--text); background: var(--surface-1); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--r-md); line-height: var(--lh-code); }
  .code-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: var(--sp-3); }
  .code-grid div { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-1); padding: var(--sp-4); background: var(--surface-1); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--r-sm); }
  .code-grid code { color: var(--brand); font-size: var(--fs-lg); font-weight: 700; }
  .code-grid span { color: var(--text-mut); font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
  .fineprint { color: var(--text-faint); font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .code-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
</style>
